\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. See the Conqueror mounts in triumph,
\par See the King in royal state
\par Riding on the clouds His chariot
\par To His heavenly palace gate;
\par Hark! the choirs of angels voices
\par Joyful hallelujahs sing,
\par And the portals high are lifted
\par To receive their heavenly King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Who is this that comes in glory,
\par With the trump of jubilee?
\par Lord of battles, God of armies,
\par He has gained the victory;
\par He who on the Cross did suffer,
\par He who from the grave arose,
\par He has vanquished sin and Satan,
\par He by death has spoiled His foes.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He has raised our human nature
\par In the clouds to God's right hand;
\par There with Him in glory stand:
\par Jesus reigns, adored by angels;
\par Man with God is on the throne;
\par Mighty Lord, in Thine ascension
\par We by faith behold our own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Glory be to God the Father;
\par Glory be to God the Son,
\par Dying, risen, ascending for us,
\par Who the heavenly realm has won;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Glory to the Holy Spirit;
\par To One God in Persons Three
\par Glory both in earth and heaven,
\par Glory, endless glory be!
\par                                 Amen!
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

